# Architecture documentation

Canonical index: `docs/architecture/README.md` (`ARCH-1001`–`ARCH-1006`; **ARCH-012** reserved).

## Do not delete

Never delete files whose path or name contains **`architecture`** (case-insensitive), including:

- `docs/architecture/**/*.md`
- `packages/features/*/src/**/*architecture*.md` (vertical supplements, e.g. `users-architecture.md`)

When consolidating doctrine, **update and link** — do not remove. Fold duplicate *behavior* into code; keep architecture docs as the authority trail.

If the user explicitly requests deletion of a specific architecture file in the current turn, confirm the path and update `docs/architecture/README.md` / cross-links in the same change.

## Where docs live

| Kind | Location |
| ---- | -------- |
| Canonical doctrine | `docs/architecture/100N-*.md` (**ARCH-1001**–**ARCH-1006**) |
| Feature vertical supplement | `packages/features/<module>/src/<area>/*-architecture.md` — links to parent ARCH doc |
| Agent routing (not doctrine) | `.cursor/hooks/afenda-architecture-routing.md` |

Do not create root-level `*-architecture.md` files outside `docs/architecture/`.

## Conflict order

**ARCH-1002** (feature packages) → **ARCH-1001** (runtime) → update the other doc in the same PR.

System Admin: **ARCH-1006** + **ARCH-1002** §7–§8 move together when control vs execution boundary changes. Kernel legacy compat is frozen (**ARCH-1002** §7).

## Target-only prose

Architecture books describe **required** shape only. Use **§7 Non-compliance** tables for wrong patterns — never “as-built vs target,” “migrate when touched,” “(target),” or “tolerated until migrated.”

`guard-architecture-compliance.mjs` **denies** writes that reintroduce lazy-doc phrases (`failClosed: true`).

## Hooks

`.cursor/hooks/guard-architecture-docs.mjs` blocks agent `Delete` on architecture paths unless the user explicitly overrides in the current task.
